sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant UI as Streamlit UI
    participant ESPN as ESPN API
    participant MO as Monitor-Orchestrator
    participant DB as SQLite
    participant W1 as Monitor Worker 1
    participant W2 as Monitor Worker 2
    participant MCP as MCP Tools
    participant SC as Upset-Scorer
    participant D3 as d3-mini Decision Model

    U->>UI: Open Condition Profiler
    UI->>ESPN: Request today's D1 vs. D1 matchups
    ESPN-->>UI: Return schedule, teams, and game statistics
    UI-->>U: Display sortable and filterable matchups

    loop Each user-initiated analysis run
        U->>UI: Select games (all by default)
        U->>UI: Click Analyze
        UI->>UI: Initialize agent progress tracker
        UI->>MO: Submit selected game IDs
        MO->>DB: Retrieve validated upset preconditions
        DB-->>MO: Return signals, thresholds, and statistics
        MO->>MO: Partition games across two workers
        MO-->>UI: Report monitoring started
        UI-->>U: Display agent progress

        par Monitor Worker 1
            MO->>W1: Assign game batch and validated signals
            loop Each assigned game
                W1->>ESPN: Retrieve current matchup data
                ESPN-->>W1: Return game statistics
                W1->>MCP: Research pregame context
                MCP-->>W1: Return cited pregame evidence
                W1->>W1: Compare evidence to validated signals
                W1->>W1: Flag matching games with citations
                W1-->>MO: Report per-game progress
                MO-->>UI: Update Worker 1 progress
            end
            W1-->>MO: Return evaluated games and flags
        and Monitor Worker 2
            MO->>W2: Assign game batch and validated signals
            loop Each assigned game
                W2->>ESPN: Retrieve current matchup data
                ESPN-->>W2: Return game statistics
                W2->>MCP: Research pregame context
                MCP-->>W2: Return cited pregame evidence
                W2->>W2: Compare evidence to validated signals
                W2->>W2: Flag matching games with citations
                W2-->>MO: Report per-game progress
                MO-->>UI: Update Worker 2 progress
            end
            W2-->>MO: Return evaluated games and flags
        end

        MO->>MO: Aggregate and deduplicate worker results
        MO-->>UI: Report monitoring complete

        alt One or more games flagged
            MO->>SC: Send flagged games and evidence
            SC->>D3: Evaluate matchup context and signals
            D3-->>SC: Return estimated upset probabilities
            SC->>SC: Rank games by predicted upset risk
            SC-->>MO: Return rankings, probabilities, and evidence
            MO-->>UI: Send ranked upset alerts
        else No games meet flagging criteria
            MO-->>UI: Return no qualifying upset alerts
        end

        UI->>UI: Mark analysis complete
        UI-->>U: Display results and supporting evidence
    end
